What does this method compute?

```java
public int countNegatives(int[] arr) {
    int count = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
        if (arr[i] < 0) {
            count++;
        }
    }
    return count;
}
```

What is returned by `findMax` when called with `{3, 9, 1, 9, 5}`?

```java
public int findMax(int[] arr) {
    int max = arr[0];
    for (int i = 1; i < arr.length; i++) {
        if (arr[i] > max) {
            max = arr[i];
        }
    }
    return max;
}
```

What does this method compute for `arr = {4, 8, 15, 16, 23}`?

```java
public double average(int[] arr) {
    int sum = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
        sum += arr[i];
    }
    return (double) sum / arr.length;
}
```

What does this method search for, and what does it return if the target isn't found?

```java
public int linearSearch(int[] arr, int target) {
    for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
        if (arr[i] == target) {
            return i;
        }
    }
    return -1;
}
```

What is wrong with this attempt to reverse an array in place?

```java
public void reverse(int[] arr) {
    for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
        int temp = arr[i];
        arr[i] = arr[arr.length - 1 - i];
        arr[arr.length - 1 - i] = temp;
    }
}
```

What does this method return for `arr = {2, 4, 6, 8}`?

```java
public boolean allEven(int[] arr) {
    for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
        if (arr[i] % 2 != 0) {
            return false;
        }
    }
    return true;
}
```

